<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Stronger His love than death and hell,</l><l>Its riches are unsearchable:</l><l>The first-born sons of light</l><l>Desire in vain its depths to see;</l><l>They cannot reach the mystery,</l><l>The length, and breadth, and height.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>God only knows the love of God;</l><l>Oh, that it now were shed abroad</l><l>In this poor stony heart;</l><l>For love I sigh, for love I pine;</l><l>This only portion, Lord, be mine,</l><l>Be mine this better part.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Oh, that I could forever sit</l><l>Like Mary, at the Master’s feet;</l><l>Be this my happy choice;</l><l>My only care, delight, and bliss,</l><l>My joy, my rest on earth be this,</l><l>To hear the Bridegroom’s voice.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
